<title>GERMANY: First German sugar beet test yield at 3.93 T/ha.</title>
<headline>First German sugar beet test yield at 3.93 T/ha.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first German sugar beet test of the 1997/98 campaign showed a sugar yield of 3.93 tonnes per hectare compared with 4.01 tonnes in the first test of 1996/97, the sugar industry association WVZ said.</p>
<p>The test also showed an average sugar content of 12.6 percent compared with 13.9 percent in the first 1996 test.  </p>
<p>The test was carried out on August 1.</p>
<p>--Scott Miller, Bonn Newsroom + 49 228 260 97150</p>
